RUN test_metadata_lock_serializes_destructive_cleanup
ok - fm-teardown: destructive cleanup serializes with metadata writers
RUN test_supported_backend_endpoint_records_validate
ok - cleanup identity: valid tmux, Herdr, Zellij, Orca, cmux, Paseo, Rex, and tern records validate, inconsistent Rex records refuse, and every empty backend target refuses
RUN test_orca_composite_worktree_id_validates
ok - cleanup identity: an Orca record's real composite worktree id validates while a separatorless or newline-carrying id refuses
RUN test_tmux_empty_target_refuses_without_invocation
ok - tmux backend: direct empty target returns nonzero without invoking tmux
RUN test_recorded_process_identity_cleanup_is_exact
ok - process cleanup: creation-time PID identity removes only the exact child and preserves the control child
RUN test_isolated_tmux_invalid_and_valid_cleanup
ok - fm-teardown: exact tmux cleanup preserves invalid and prefix-matched neighbors while removing only the recorded target
RUN test_failed_endpoint_close_refuses_before_removing_the_record
ok - fm-teardown: a close that genuinely failed refuses and keeps the record naming the surviving endpoint, and the same teardown finishes once the close works
RUN test_forced_teardown_continues_past_a_close_it_could_not_make
ok - fm-teardown: --force continues past a close it could not make while still reporting it, and the same case refuses without --force
RUN test_unreadable_close_read_refuses_while_a_definitive_absence_completes
ok - fm-teardown: a close re-read that could not run refuses, while a definitively absent session or server still completes silently
RUN test_forced_secondmate_child_close_failure_still_refuses
not ok - the refusal did not name the child whose endpoint could not be closed
